[RTCT.6.2] **Body proto** (`proto/realtime_contract.proto`):

```proto
message RealtimeContract {
  uint32 wm_max               = 1;
  uint32 agenda_cap           = 2;
  uint32 max_fires_per_pump   = 3;
  uint32 token_pool_cap       = 4;
  uint32 intern_cap           = 5;
  uint32 intern_bytes_cap     = 6;
  uint64 pump_wcet_ns         = 7;
  repeated NodeCap   nodes    = 8;    // LEGACY per-node list; ascending node_id.
                                      // Emitted only when a producer chooses the
                                      // legacy encoding (see [RTCT.6.7.5]).
  repeated SeriesCap series   = 9;    // ascending series_id
  bytes  rt_config_sha256     = 10;   // 32 raw bytes, the canonical hash

  // Compact node-cap encoding (gated on realtime; see [RTCT.6.7]).
  uint32 node_count        = 11;      // covered network nodes (cross-check)
  uint32 default_node_cap  = 12;      // capacity for every covered node not overridden
  repeated NodeCapOverride node_overrides  = 13;   // sparse, ascending node_id
  repeated uint32          node_caps_packed = 14 [packed = true];  // dense fallback

  // Cache caps (gated on realtime; see [RTCT.6.8]).
  uint32 cache_cap         = 15;      // max live cache keys (<= 2^31-1)
  uint64 cache_bytes_cap   = 16;      // cache value byte capacity (<= 2^63-1)

  // Json caps (see [RTCT.6.10]); 0 = the fixed maximum of [LGRA.5.8.6].
  uint32 json_depth_cap        = 17;
  uint32 json_node_cap         = 18;
  uint32 json_string_bytes_cap = 19;
  uint32 json_text_bytes_cap   = 20;
}

message NodeCap {
  uint32 node_id   = 1;
  string kind      = 2;                // "alpha"|"beta"|"term"
  uint32 capacity  = 3;
}

message NodeCapOverride {
  uint32 node_id   = 1;
  uint32 capacity  = 2;
}

message SeriesCap {
  uint32 series_id = 1;
  uint32 capacity  = 2;
}
```

The `nodes` (field 8) legacy list and the compact fields (11–14) are two
encodings of the same logical per-node capacity map; a contract uses **exactly
one** ([RTCT.6.7]). `node_count`/`default_node_cap`/`node_overrides`/
`node_caps_packed` carry no `kind` — the runtime derives each node's kind from
its `AlphaNode`/`BetaNode`/`TerminalNode` atom ([RBND.4b.8]).
